#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:2
msgid "Writing direction and reading order"
msgstr "书写方向与朗读顺序"

#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:4
msgid "A pane has two writing directions. The inline direction advances one logical column. The line direction advances one logical row. Programs choose both with OSC 777. Glyphs and images stay upright."
msgstr "每个窗格有两个书写方向。行内方向决定逻辑列的递增方向，换行方向决定逻辑行的递增方向。程序可通过 OSC 777 选择这两个方向。字形和图像始终正立。"

#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:8
msgid "Set :opt:`text_flow` in ``silkie.conf``, for example ``text_flow down left``. Programs can override it for the duration of an interaction."
msgstr "在 ``silkie.conf`` 中设置 :opt:`text_flow`，例如 ``text_flow down left``。程序可在交互期间覆盖此设置。"

#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:11
msgid "For example, this shell command writes two columns of Chinese. The first starts at the top right. The second appears immediately to its left::"
msgstr "例如，以下 shell 命令输出两列中文。第一列从右上角开始，第二列紧靠其左侧::"

#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:16
msgid "The logical home position is row 1, column 1. Changing direction keeps the cursor with the content, so the example explicitly homes the cursor. At the last logical line, another line feed scrolls the contents toward the first line. Scrollback retains the logical lines. Switching between horizontal and vertical writing reflows the pane to its new dimensions."
msgstr "逻辑起点是第 1 行第 1 列。切换方向时光标随内容移动，因此示例显式将光标移回起点。在最后一个逻辑行继续换行，内容便向第一行滚动。回滚缓冲区保留逻辑行。横写与竖写之间切换时，窗格按新尺寸重新排版。"

