#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:63
msgid "Coordinates"
msgstr "坐标"

#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:65
msgid "Cursor addressing, wrapping, margins, selection, image placements and mouse cell reports use the logical grid. A carriage return goes to its first column. Programs can query the dimensions with CSI 18 t or the PTY window size. Wide characters still occupy two inline cells. A placement's columns span the inline axis and its rows span the line axis. Image source rectangles use the original image's pixel coordinates."
msgstr "光标寻址、自动折行、边距、选区、图像放置和鼠标单元格报告均使用逻辑网格。回车移至当前逻辑行的首列。程序可通过 CSI 18 t 或伪终端的窗口尺寸查询网格大小。宽字符仍占两个行内单元格。图像放置的列数沿行内方向延伸，行数沿换行方向延伸。图像源矩形使用原图像素坐标。"

#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:72
msgid "Pane-relative pixel positions in mouse, scroll, gesture, tablet tool and direct-touch reports use the writing axes. Device-surface coordinates, including indirect touch positions, describe the hardware. A captured contact is cancelled in its old coordinates before the axes change."
msgstr "鼠标、滚动、手势、数位笔及直接触摸报告中的窗格相对像素位置使用书写坐标轴。设备表面坐标（包括间接触摸位置）描述硬件本身。更改坐标轴前，会按原坐标取消已捕获的接触点。"

#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:78
msgid "Reading order"
msgstr "朗读顺序"

#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:80
msgid "An application can direct screen reader navigation independently of writing direction. Set the direction **before** writing the character whose successor it describes. For example, write a label above its value and have the reader continue down from the last character of the label::"
msgstr "应用程序可独立于书写方向指定屏幕阅读器的导航顺序。应在写入字符 **之前** 设置方向，指定阅读器接下来应移向哪个相邻字符。例如，可在值的上方绘制标签，并让阅读器在读完标签的最后一个字符后向下继续::"

#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:88
msgid "The hint stays active for subsequent writes. Each character retains its hint through scrolling and reflow. Overwriting the character replaces its hint. Use ``right``, ``left``, ``down``, or ``up`` for a physical direction and ``auto`` for ordinary logical order."
msgstr "提示对后续写入的字符持续生效。滚动和重新排版会保留每个字符的提示。覆盖字符会替换其提示。使用 ``right``、``left``、``down`` 或 ``up`` 指定屏幕上的实际方向，使用 ``auto`` 按常规逻辑顺序朗读。"

msgid "Use ``next=end`` before writing the last character to include it and end the pane’s accessible text there. For example, the following displays ``Done. Extra`` and exposes ``Done.`` to the screen reader::"
msgstr "在写入最后一个字符前设置 ``next=end``，阅读器会读出该字符，并在此结束窗格的无障碍文本。例如，以下命令显示 ``Done. Extra``，屏幕阅读器只读出 ``Done.``::"

msgid "The reader starts at chain heads in logical order, then visits any remaining cycles. A link to a blank or past the viewport edge ends that chain. The reader tracks every character position it has emitted during this read. If a link points to any of those positions, reading stops immediately, before repeating the character or starting another chain. Direct speech requests continue to speak the supplied string."
msgstr "阅读器按逻辑顺序从各链的起点开始，随后访问余下的环路。链接指向空白单元格或超出视口边界时，当前链结束。阅读器记录本次已读出的每个字符的位置。如果链接指向任何已读位置，朗读会立即结束，不会重复该字符，也不会开始下一条链。直接语音请求仍朗读所提供的字符串。"

#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:97
msgid "Protocol"
msgstr "协议"

#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:99
msgid "Discover support through the entry ``flow.1`` in :doc:`capabilities-protocol`. Frames follow :doc:`extension-framing`. The default is ``inline=right``, ``line=down``, ``next=auto``."
msgstr "通过 :doc:`capabilities-protocol` 中的 ``flow.1`` 条目探测支持情况。帧格式遵循 :doc:`extension-framing`。默认设置为 ``inline=right``、``line=down``、``next=auto``。"

#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:103
msgid "``op=set:inline=DIRECTION:line=DIRECTION`` sets both writing axes. They must be perpendicular."
msgstr "``op=set:inline=DIRECTION:line=DIRECTION`` 设置两个书写轴，方向必须相互垂直。"

#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:105
msgid "``op=reading:next=DIRECTION`` changes the hint for subsequent writes."
msgstr "``op=reading:next=DIRECTION`` 设置后续写入字符的朗读提示。"

#: docs/silkie/flow-protocol.rst:106
msgid "``op=query:id=N`` returns the current settings. Either setter also accepts an optional request ID and replies with the resulting settings."
msgstr "``op=query:id=N`` 返回当前设置。两种设置命令也可携带请求 ID，以获取设置结果。"

